    <bpmn:process id="W_W1745" name="W1745. New Store Budget Tracking &amp; Variance Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Project charter approved (W1737)
Frequency: Continuous through project completion; final reconciliation post-opening
Volume: 1 budget per new store (~PHP 40–60M)
Owner: FP&amp;A
Participants: FP&amp;A, Store Opening Coordinator, CFO, VP Store Operations
Source: workflow W1745 — New Store Budget Tracking &amp; Variance Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1745_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1745_Lane1" name="FP&amp;A">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1745_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1745_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1745_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1745_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1745_Lane2" name="Store Opening Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1745_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1745_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1745_Start4" name="Project charter approved (W1737)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1745_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1745_Task5" name="FP&amp;A establishes project budget per financial model from W1652: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: FP&amp;A establishes project budget per financial model from W1652: (a) construction/renovation (~60% of budget), (b) fixtures and equipment (~15%), (c) initial inventory (~35–40%, aligned to W1739&#x27;s ~PHP 15–25M initial stock), (d) IT infrastructure (~5%), (e) marketing/grand opening (~2%), (f) staff recruitment and training (~2%), (g) permits and fees (~1%)
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1745_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1745_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1745_Task6" name="Monthly: FP&amp;A tracks actual costs against budget: (a) committed costs (POs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly: FP&amp;A tracks actual costs against budget: (a) committed costs (POs issued but not yet invoiced), (b) incurred costs (invoices received and paid), (c) forecast to complete (remaining budget needed), (d) total forecast vs. original budget
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 hours/month/project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1745_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1745_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1745_Task7" name="Variance management: (a) &lt; 5% variance: Store Opening Coordinator adjusts…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Variance management: (a) &lt; 5% variance: Store Opening Coordinator adjusts within project, (b) 5–10% variance: VP Store Operations approval required, (c) &gt; 10% variance: CFO and COO approval; steering committee informed; corrective action plan required
Responsible (R): Store Opening Coordinator / VP Store Operations / CFO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: As needed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1745_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1745_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1745_Task8" name="Post-opening reconciliation: FP&amp;A finalizes project cost; reconciles to capex…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Post-opening reconciliation: FP&amp;A finalizes project cost; reconciles to capex project per W40.3; CIP converted to fixed assets; pre-opening expenses (training, marketing, trial runs) expensed per PFRS
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A / Fixed Asset Accountant
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–4 weeks post-opening</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1745_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1745_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1745_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1745_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-352 (ensure controlled execution — New Store Project Planning &amp; Coordination (PA-37.1).) | - operational: FP&amp;A review and approval gate; periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: FP&amp;A</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
